<article class="env-example" id="05Z6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05Z6">Example <span data-tag="05Z6">67.53.3</span>.</a> This is a continuation of Remark <a href="/tag/05VS" data-tag="05VS">67.19.4</a>. Consider the algebraic space $X = \mathbf{A}^1_ k/\{ x \sim -x \mid x \not= 0\} $. There are morphisms </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathbf{A}^1_ k \longrightarrow X \longrightarrow \mathbf{A}^1_ k  \]
</div>
  <p> such that the first arrow is étale surjective, the second arrow is universally injective, and the composition is the map $x \mapsto x^2$. Hence the composition is universally closed. Thus it follows that the map $X \to \mathbf{A}^1_ k$ is a universal homeomorphism, but $X \to \mathbf{A}^1_ k$ is not separated. </p>
</article>